    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, then map points to a level, exposing both fields.\n\n**`MembershipLevels.java`** \u2014 reworked into two methods:\n- `points(Owner)`: starts at 0, adds 2 for an email, 1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, 2 for a household of 3+, and 3 for tenure over 365 days.\n- `of(Owner)`: maps points to level \u2014 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping alongside the existing `membershipLevel` mapping, so the response DTO carries both.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel`'s description/range (now 1\u20134). The generated `OwnerDto` picks up the new field at build time.\n\n`AuditOwnerCreated` continues to work via `MembershipLevels.of(owner)`.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsPointsAndLevel`) confirms a fresh owner with an email and no namesake scores 3 points \u2192 level 2, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
