    "probe_text": "Done \u2014 I've traced the whole `POST /api/owners` pipeline (`owners.POST.yml` plus every function class it names). Here is everything that happens, in execution order. Every step runs inside a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the very end.\n\n## Gate (whole endpoint)\n- **Authorization:** `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` (handled \u2192 403).\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` (validations + normalizing side-effects on the request body)\nIn this exact order:\n1. **Normalize `address`** in place: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). (Done first so the blank check sees the normalized value.)\n2. **Required-field check** on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` \u2014 any null/blank (after address normalization) \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**, naming the missing fields).\n3. **Normalize `telephone` to E.164** and store it back on the body \u2014 strip separators, keep explicit `+CC` or assume `+61` and drop a leading `0`; require 8\u201315 digits and, for recognized codes, exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (**400**).\n4. **Normalize `email`** (only if present/non-blank): must match the email pattern (else `InvalidOwnerEmailException`, **400**); lower-cased in place; domain must not be a disposable-domain blocklist member (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) else `DisposableOwnerEmailException` (**400**). Absent email is allowed.\n5. **Validate `postcode`** (only if present): must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` (**400**). Absent postcode allowed.\n6. **Reject future `registrationDate`**: if supplied and after the server date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n7. Publish the validated/normalized body for later steps.\n\n## 2. `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity` (validation)\nCompute deterministic `householdId` from (normalized lastName, postcode). If any existing owner already carries that id \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**). Skipped when the `sharesHousehold` flag is true, or when there is no postcode.\n\n## 3. `EnsureCityCapacity` (validation)\nIf the request's city already holds **\u2265 50** owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**). (New owner not yet counted.)\n\n## 4. `EnsureDailyCreateLimit` (validation)\nRoll the effective registration date (supplied, else today) forward to a business day; if **\u2265 100** owners already carry that business day \u2192 `DailyCreateLimitException` (**429**).\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner` (side-effect: construct entity)\nMap the DTO to an `Owner`, then set `registrationDate` = the effective date (supplied or today) adjusted forward off weekends to the next Monday.\n\n## 6. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` (side-effect)\nSet `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, REGION from postcode/city, HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256(canonical telephone + lastName).\n\n## 7. `AssignOwnerHousehold` (side-effect)\nSet `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(normalized lastName | postcode), or null when no postcode.\n\n## 8. `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` (side-effect)\nSet `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same firstName + lastName (case-insensitive), computed **before** save (new owner excluded).\n\n## 9. `SaveOwner` (side-effect: persist)\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 assigns the id.\n\n## 10. `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect: logging)\nEmit an `AUDIT` logger line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel.\n\n## 11. `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning` (side-effect)\nSet `bulkSignupWarning` = true when **> 80** owners share the registration date. Runs after save so the new owner is counted.\n\n## 12. `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` (side-effect)\nSet `householdSize` = number of owners sharing the `householdId` (including this one; 1 when no household). Drives the GOLD tier (\u2265 3). Runs after save.\n\n## 13. `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate` (side-effect, transient)\nSet `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`: flags a soft match \u2014 same lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but different canonical telephone, excluding fellow household members and itself; records the lowest-id match. Not persisted (set after save on the returned object).\n\n## 14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\nRespond **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\nThen the surrounding transaction commits once.\n\nA few things worth flagging as you read this: steps 11\u201313 run **after** `SaveOwner`, so their counts include the just-created owner (this is deliberate \u2014 it matches what a later GET recomputes). And `namesakeCount` (step 8) runs **before** save, so it deliberately does not. `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are computed but never persisted \u2014 they only decorate the create response."
